 "teach": {
  "tracking": {
   "name": "Reading tracks",
   "how": "Maren shows you how to read a trail: how deep a print sinks, how fast its edges crumble, which way the toes point. You can now see fresh footprints and tell who is following you."
  }
 },
 "about_asks": "People ask for things they really want (scenes.*.people[].asks). A relic ask is done by handing over the real object (act gift-<relic>); they pay from their side's cache, so what they can give runs out. A pointer ask ('about' another person) is never ticked off: they only know it is done when the person comes home and tells them, or they saw it. A 'repeat' ask (fish) is open every time: each fish is one gift, remembered like any other, paid from the camp's real stock, and it adds to that camp's food."
}
